<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Velvet Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Velvet Revolution was the peaceful overthrow of communist rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> in November and December 1989. Mass demonstrations began after police beat students in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> on 17 November, and a general strike forced the Communist Party to give up its monopoly of power. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaclav-havel">Václav Havel</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civic-forum">Civic Forum</a> was elected president on 29 December, and free elections followed in 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/velvet-revolution.jpg" alt="Velvet Revolution" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ŠJů (cs:ŠJů) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Praha_1989-11-25,_Letn%C3%A1,_dav_(01).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
